        "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
        "senderName": "NWS San Diego CA",
        "headline": "Beach Hazards Statement issued November 10 at 2:18AM PST until November 10 at 10:00PM PST by NWS San Diego CA",
        "description": "* WHAT...Minor to locally moderate coastal flooding expected.\nAdditionally, dangerous rip currents and surf of 3 to 7 feet\nexpected along west-facing beaches.\n\n* WHERE...San Diego County Coastal Areas.\n\n* WHEN...For the Coastal Flood Advisory, until noon PST today. For\nthe Beach Hazards Statement, through this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of parking lots and roads with only\nisolated road closures expected. Dangerous swimming conditions\ndue to elevated surf and strong rip currents.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...High tide at 833 AM today is expected to\npeak over 7 feet MLLW, which is 1.2 to 1.4 feet above\nastronomical tide predictions.",
        "instruction": "If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be\nclosed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of\nunknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone\nproperty.\n\nInexperienced swimmers should remain out of the water to avoid\nhazardous swimming conditions.",
        "response": "Avoid",
